A larger ratio is not automatically better or worse. If the numerator is a fixed ground-truth baseline and the denominator is the repetition you want to minimize, then a larger ratio is generally better because it means the denominator is smaller relative to the baseline. But if the numerator can vary, a larger ratio may simply mean the ground-truth-prefix repetition got worse, so the ratio alone is not a reliable target; for minimizing repetition, directly minimize the denominator or the absolute repetition.
